# gitleaks ignore list: one fingerprint per reviewed finding, in the form
# <commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>. A fingerprint pins exactly one historical
# finding, so a new secret in the same file, or the same value re-added in a
# later commit, still fails the scan.
#
# Before adding an entry, confirm the value grants access to nothing. A real
# credential gets revoked first, and its entry says so. For a false positive
# that is still present at HEAD, prefer an inline `gitleaks:allow` comment on
# the line itself, so push/PR scans stay quiet if the line is edited or moved.

